📅 Day 17 – Exception Handling in Java

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on Exception Handling in Java and its importance in building reliable and robust applications. The mentor explained how runtime errors can interrupt program execution and how exceptions help in handling such situations gracefully.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Introduction to Exceptions

An exception is an unwanted event that occurs during program execution.

Exceptions disrupt the normal flow of the program.

Java provides a mechanism to handle errors using exception handling constructs.

2️⃣ Exception Handling Keywords

The structure of exception handling includes:

✅ try

Contains code that may cause an exception.

✅ catch

Handles the exception thrown in the try block.

✅ finally

Executes regardless of whether an exception occurs or not.

✅ throw

Used to explicitly throw an exception.

✅ throws

Declares exceptions that a method may generate.

3️⃣ Types of Exceptions

The session covered two main categories:

🔹 Checked Exceptions

Checked at compile time.

Example: IOException, SQLException.

🔹 Unchecked Exceptions

Occur at runtime.

Example: ArithmeticException, NullPointerException.

4️⃣ Practical Implementation

Wrote programs to handle ArithmeticException (e.g., division by zero).

Practiced handling input-related exceptions.

Observed how try-catch blocks prevent program crashes.

🎯 Learning Outcomes

